  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## The recordings\n\n- **mmj2012-03-29.mbho604** (recommended): matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 20 songs; 138 min; rated 5/5 by 1 [1]. Said about its sound: The reviewer prefers the fuller sound of the MBHO recording over other versions [6]\n- **mmj2012-03-29.m200.flac16**: matrix (soundboard mixed with audience mics); 20 songs; 137 min [2]\n- **mmj2012-03-29.dpa4023**: source not stated; 20 songs; 138 min; rated 5/5 by 2 [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Guests Yomoda Naohito and Hirose Takao played trumpet and trombone on this track [2]\n- A Japanese horn section appeared on Victory Dance, Dancefloors, and One Big Holiday [3]\n- The previous Nagoya show was canceled due to Jim's throat problem [3]\n- The horn section was positioned in front of the mixing board [3]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **mmj2012-03-29.mbho604**: taped by 1046; transferred by 1046; source: Taper's Section @ Right Front Of SBD Center MBHO MBO 604 / KA 200N > V2 > SONY PCM D50 (WAv 24 bit / 48 kHz) [1]\n- **mmj2012-03-29.m200.flac16**: taped by Koji; transferred by Koji; source: Taper's Section @ Left Front Of SBD Center Microtech Gefell M200's>Attenuator -20dB>MixPre>PCM-M10(44.1kHz 16Bit) [2]\n- **mmj2012-03-29.dpa4023**: taped by GAKU TANIGUCHI (trailights record / tapersdelight); transferred by GAKU TANIGUCHI (trailights record / tapersdelight); source: DPA4023 > SONOSAX SX-M2 > KORG MR-1000(WSD 5.6448MHz /1bit) [3]",
